Search quality. No cell is missing. 21 of the 98 doubling checks are flagged, and fresh-market
factorial cells outside Q1 and Q4 have no doubling check, so their narrow intervals describe seed
noise only. The report lists the search-flagged cells, and the addendum traces the inherited flags of
every Q1 and Q4 decision through the records’ references. Q2 and Q3 statements are descriptive;
the cells they use carry the flags listed in the report. Table 19 sets the Q1 estimates beside their
re-evaluation with the registered configurations, and Table 20 compares the Q4 estimates, calibrated
lower bounds, and decisions under both configurations and gives the adjusted market p-value under
the registered configuration; the largest Q4 change is on fresh4, where the gain difference moves
from 0.183 to 0.176, still above the registered 0.10.

